[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Given an array of citations (each citation is a non-negative integer) of a researcher, write a function to compute the researcher's h-index.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m According to the definition of h-index on Wikipedia: "A scientist has index h if h of his/her N papers have at least h citations each, and the other N − h papers have no more than h citations each."
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
