[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m In the first sample Luke should stay exactly in the middle of the segment, that is at coordinates [2;4], as the presses move with the same speed.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m In the second sample he needs to occupy the position $[ 2 \frac{2}{3} ; 3 \frac{2}{3} ]$. In this case both presses move to his edges at the same time.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Assistant: Let me solve this step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m <think>First, we need to find the time it takes for the presses to meet. We can do this by dividing the distance between the presses by the sum of their speeds. This will give us the time it takes for the presses to meet, which is the time Luke can stay alive. </think>
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m <answer>
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m def max_time_alive(d, L, v1, v2):
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m     time_to_meet = (L - d) / (v1 + v2)
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m     return time_to_meet
