[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m You are given an integer N. Among the integers between 1 and N (inclusive), how many Shichi-Go-San numbers (literally "Seven-Five-Three numbers") are there?
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Here, a Shichi-Go-San number is a positive integer that satisfies the following condition:
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m  - When the number is written in base ten, each of the digits 7, 5 and 3 appears at least once, and the other digits never appear.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m -----Constraints-----
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m  - 1 \leq N < 10^9
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m  - N is an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m -----Input-----
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m N
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m -----Output-----
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Print the number of the Shichi-Go-San numbers between 1 and N (inclusive).
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m -----Sample Input-----
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 575
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m -----Sample Output-----
