[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m User: Write a Python function to solve the following problem. Show your reasoning in <think> </think> tags. Return only the function code in <answer> </answer> tags.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Stanley and Megan decided to shop in the "Crossmarket" grocery store, which can be represented as a matrix with $n$ rows and $m$ columns.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Stanley and Megan can move to an adjacent cell using $1$ unit of power. Two cells are considered adjacent if they share an edge. To speed up the shopping process, Megan brought her portals with her, and she leaves one in each cell she visits (if there is no portal yet). If a person (Stanley or Megan) is in a cell with a portal, that person can use $1$ unit of power to teleport to any other cell with a portal, including Megan's starting cell.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m They decided to split up: Stanley will go from the upper-left cell (cell with coordinates $(1, 1)$) to the lower-right cell (cell with coordinates $(n, m)$), whilst Megan needs to get from the lower-left cell (cell with coordinates $(n, 1)$) to the upper-right cell (cell with coordinates $(1, m)$).
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m What is the minimum total energy needed for them both to do that?
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Note that they can choose the time they move. Time does not affect energy.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
