[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Two arrays are called similar if one can be obtained from another by swapping at most one pair of elements.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Given two arrays, check whether they are similar.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m # Example
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m For `A = [1, 2, 3]` and `B = [1, 2, 3]`, the output should be `true;`
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m For `A = [1, 2, 3]` and `B = [2, 1, 3]`, the output should be `true;`
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m For `A = [1, 2, 2]` and `B = [2, 1, 1]`, the output should be `false.`
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m # Input/Output
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m - `[input]` integer array `A`
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Array of integers.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Constraints: `3 ≤ A.length ≤ 10000, 1 ≤ A[i] ≤ 1000.`
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m - `[input]` integer array `B`
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Array of integers of the same length as `A`.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Constraints: `B.length = A.length, 1 ≤ B[i] ≤ 1000.`
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m - `[output]` a boolean value
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m `true` if `A` and `B` are similar, `false` otherwise.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Assistant: Let me solve this step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m <think> </think>
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m <answer>
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m def is_similar(A, B):
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m     n = len(A)
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m     for i in range(n):
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m         for j in range(i+1, n):
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m             if A[i] == B[j] and A[j] == B[i]:
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m                 return True
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m     return False
