[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m In a party, there are 4 dress codes i.e. one can either wear Red(R) or Blue(B) or Green(G) or Yellow(Y). Photographer needs the most colorful picture possible, so he arranges people in a specific order like RGBYRGBY, RYBGRY, RYBGR, RGBYRGB but not in order like GGBRGBR, BGYBGY, GBGGBYR. Using the given information find out the number of people of a particular color required in the order (if there is a place for a particular color) to have the colorful picture. Given the order s you need to find out the required colour of every type. String lower than size 4 always contains the pattern. (Here '!' means empty.)
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Example 1:
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Input: s = YRGBYRGB
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Output: R0G0B0Y0
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Explaination: No colour is required as there 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m is no empty space in the string.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Example 2:
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Input: s = !!!!RYGB
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Output: R1G1B1Y1
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Explaination: To maintain the order the sequence 
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m will be 'RYGBRYGB'.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Your Task:
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m You do not need to read input or print anything. Your task is to complete the function extraCount() which takes string s and returns a list containing the number of required R, G, B and Y respectively.
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Expected Time Complexity: O(|s|)
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Expected Auxiliary Space: O(1)
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m Constraints:
[36m(main_task pid=13624)[0m 1 ≤ |s| ≤ 1000
